What is the output?

Two loops each start with `n = 10` and use the condition `n < 5`:
```js
while (n < 5) { document.write(n); n++; }

do { document.write(n); n++; } while (n < 5);
```
Which statement is correct?

Which numbers are written by this code?
```js
var x = 1;
while (x < 20) {
  if (x == 5) { break; }
  x = x + 1;
  document.write(x + " ");
}
```

Which statement describes the output of this code?
```js
var x = 1;
while (x < 10) {
  x = x + 1;
  if (x == 5) { continue; }
  document.write(x + " ");
}
```

How many times is `x` written by this code?
```js
outerloop:
for (var i = 0; i < 5; i++) {
  innerloop:
  for (var j = 0; j < 5; j++) {
    if (j > 3) break;
    if (i == 2) break innerloop;
    if (i == 4) break outerloop;
    document.write("x");
  }
}
```

